Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an inheritance task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: The inheritance layer is broken. Make the child type inherit correctly, initialize base state, and override the inherited behavior.

Current code in the editor:
```
class Animal {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }

  speak() {
    return this.name + " makes a sound";
  }
}

class Dog {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }
}

```

Generate 1 code variant that looks like real work but uses bad practices or is subtly inefficient. The code_snippet should be the full file content. The bad_practice should explain in 1-2 sentences why this code is problematic.

hints.code_snippet:
class Animal {
  constructor(name) {
    this.name = name;
  }

  speak() {
    return this.name + " makes a sound";
  }
}

class Dog extends Animal {
  constructor(name) {
    super(name);
    this.breed = "Labrador"; 
  }

  speak() {
    // Retrieving the generic animal sound and then modifying it
    const genericSound = super.speak();
    if (genericSound.includes("makes a sound")) {
      return genericSound.replace("makes a sound", "barks");
    } else {
      // Fallback for unexpected generic sounds
      return this.name + " barks";
    }
  }
}

